1
00:05:16,363 --> 00:05:22,363
Everyone in the world has forgotten The Beatles. Everyone except Jack…

2
00:10:32,727 --> 00:10:38,727
Yesterday is a comedy, fantasy, music film directed by Danny Boyle.

3
00:15:49,090 --> 00:15:55,090
A struggling musician realizes he's the only person on Earth who can remember The Beatles
after waking up in an alternate reality where the group was forgotten.

4
00:21:05,454 --> 00:21:11,454
Jack Malik, played by Himesh Patel.

5
00:26:21,818 --> 00:26:27,818
Ellie Appleton, played by Lily James.

6
00:31:38,181 --> 00:31:44,181
Carol, played by Sophia Di Martino.

7
00:36:54,545 --> 00:37:00,545
Lucy, played by Ellise Chappell.

8
00:42:10,909 --> 00:42:16,909
Sheila Malik, played by Meera Syal.

9
00:47:27,272 --> 00:47:33,272
Nick, played by Harry Michell.

10
00:52:43,636 --> 00:52:49,636
Yesterday is a 2019 jukebox musical romantic comedy film directed by Danny Boyle and
written by Richard Curtis based on a story by Jack Barth and Curtis.

11
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Himesh Patel stars as struggling musician Jack Malik, who suddenly finds himself as the only
person who remembers the Beatles and becomes famous for performing their songs.

12
01:03:16,363 --> 01:03:22,363
The film also stars Lily James, Joel Fry, Ed Sheeran, and Kate McKinnon.

13
01:08:32,727 --> 01:08:38,727
Yesterday was announced in March 2018.

14
01:13:49,090 --> 01:13:55,090
Filming began the following month around England,
particularly Norfolk and Halesworth in Suffolk.

15
01:19:05,454 --> 01:19:11,454
Photography also took place at Wembley Stadium, the
Principality Stadium, and in Los Angeles.

16
01:24:21,818 --> 01:24:27,818
The filmmakers paid $10 million for the rights to use the Beatles' music.

17
01:29:38,181 --> 01:29:44,181
Although none of the band members were involved, Boyle received
approval for the project from them or their families.

18
01:34:54,545 --> 01:35:00,545
Yesterday had its world premiere at the Tribeca Film Festival on 4 May 2019, and was released in
the United Kingdom and the United States on 28 June 2019 by Universal Pictures.

19
01:40:10,909 --> 01:40:16,909
The film grossed $154.6 million worldwide against a
production budget of $26 million.

20
01:45:27,272 --> 01:45:33,272
The film explores themes of musician, pop singer,
liverpool, england, music festival, united kingdom.

21
01:50:43,636 --> 01:50:49,636
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
